{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>You shall not wrong a stranger.</b> Verbal wronging — קונטרארי\"ר בְּלַעַז — as in ״וְהַאֲכַלְתִּי אֶת מוֹנַיִךְ אֶת בְּשָׂרָם״ (Isaiah 49)." "<b>Nor shall you oppress him.</b> By robbery of money." "<b>For you were strangers.</b> If you wronged him, he too can wrong you and say to you: You too came as a stranger — 'the blemish that is in you, do not say to your fellow.' Every expression of גֵּר means a person who was not born in that country, but came from another country to sojourn there."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French contre dire, 'to contradict / taunt with words'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:57.897875189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}